{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":47394,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"603c177d-ca99-5e0d-aa14-9bef9015bf9e","total_cost_usd":0.24765499999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":12650,"output_tokens":4506,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4506,"cache_read_input_tokens":12650,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9600,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.009685,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":4506,"cacheReadInputTokens":12650,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.23796999999999996,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:stage1-recovery-fable-01\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:35069763f06891dba5a3\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"The selected result claims an occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network (96 stations per the stated target population and task), but computes 18/72 using only the 72 stations retained after the signal screen as the exposure denominator, so a retained-subset denominator is used for a complete-domain claim.\", \"root_cause\": \"The workflow hard-codes SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72 as the denominator in the selected-result line while the report's own scientific target and the task both define the complete domain as all 96 scheduled stations; the 24 screen-omitted scheduled stations are dropped from exposure without any protocol amendment or conditional restatement of the claim.\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Task requires one rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Report states the target population is all 96 scheduled stations.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 4, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Selected result claims the entire-network rate but divides by 72 retained stations.\", \"observed_value\": \"18/72 = 0.25 labeled as entire-network rate\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Workflow constructs the selected line with SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (72) as denominator.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Data confirm 96 scheduled rows with 24 omitted stations excluded from the retained set; example omitted scheduled station.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Falsification attempt: checked whether any protocol amendment or approved deviation authorizes restricting the domain to the retained subset; the report explicitly denies one exists, so no authorized conditional restatement rescues the claim.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 18, \"end_line\": 18, \"quoted_text\": \"No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Checked whether the claim could be read as conditional on the retained subset; the denominator line names the retained subset, but the selected-result sentence itself asserts the rate is 'for the entire scheduled survey network', so the conditional reading fails.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 11, \"end_line\": 11, \"quoted_text\": \"Occurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to falsify the issue by (a) reading the selected result as explicitly conditional on the retained subset and (b) searching for a protocol amendment permitting the subset domain. Both fail: the selected-result line (results/report.md L15) labels 18/72 as the rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network', matching the stated 96-station target (L4) and task, and L18 denies any amendment or approved deviation. I also verified the numbers against inputs/data.csv: 96 data rows, 24 rows with screen_status=omitted, 18 rows with occurrence_flag=1 among retained rows, confirming 72 is the retained subset, not the complete domain of 96.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Task explicitly defines the scientific question as conditional on passing the signal screen, making the 72-station eligible set the intended domain.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Selected result is explicitly scoped to the signal-eligible subset and uses the matching 72 denominator.\", \"observed_value\": \"18/72 = 25% among signal-eligible stations\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Report states the target population as the 72 eligible stations, consistent with the conditional task.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 4, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Input data are aggregated counts consistent with 18 + 54 = 72 eligible and 24 outside-eligible stations.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"signal_eligible_occurrence,18,observed\\nsignal_eligible_no_occurrence,54,not_observed\\noutside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Falsification attempt: checked whether the report anywhere claims a complete-network (96-station) rate that would make the 72 denominator a subset mismatch; the only mention of 96 is descriptive network context, and the 24 outside-eligible stations are explicitly declared outside the target and not assessed, so no complete-domain claim exists.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 3, \"end_line\": 3, \"quoted_text\": \"Scheduled network: 96 stations.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"Planned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to demonstrate the in-scope issue by looking for any claim asserting a rate over the complete 96-station scheduled network paired with the 72-station denominator. None exists: the selected result (results/report.md L8) is worded 'Among signal-eligible stations', the target population line (L4) restricts scope to the 72 eligible stations, and the task itself (task.md L1) asks for the rate conditional on passing the screen. Per the scope definition, a target explicitly conditional on the retained subset is not this issue; arithmetic 18/72 = 25% is internally consistent with the input counts (18 + 54 = 72).\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Task asks for a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled network.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Selected result uses the complete 96-station scheduled denominator matching the stated complete-domain claim.\", \"observed_value\": \"18/96 = 0.1875 (18.75 per 100 scheduled stations)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Workflow hard-codes the scheduled-station denominator in the selected line.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Report explicitly states no screened-subset rate is reported and all claims use the 96 denominator.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 19, \"end_line\": 19, \"quoted_text\": \"No screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Falsification attempt: checked whether the 24 unobserved omitted stations (occurrence_flag NA) make the 96 denominator a disguised subset problem; the report acknowledges the unobserved status and bounds the claim as a lower bound, and the in-scope issue class concerns only a retained-subset denominator used for a complete-domain claim, which does not occur here since the denominator is the full 96.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 18, \"end_line\": 18, \"quoted_text\": \"The 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate.\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to demonstrate the in-scope issue by searching for any selected rate that pairs a complete-domain claim with the 72-station retained-subset denominator. The selected result (results/report.md L15) instead divides 18 by all 96 scheduled stations, matching the stated target population (L4: all 96 scheduled stations) and the task. I verified against inputs/data.csv that there are 96 scheduled data rows and 18 rows with occurrence_flag=1, and that 18/96 = 0.1875 as reported. Treating the 24 NA stations as zero occurrences is a distinct methodological choice, but it is explicitly disclosed as a lower bound (L18) and is not the declared retained-subset-denominator issue class.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":6348,"ttft_stream_ms":1783,"time_to_request_ms":9,"type":"result","duration_ms":46548,"uuid":"7c022fd8-a6f5-4988-8680-9cce45026db5"}
